Many will have noticed that when, say, an arrow or
dart trap shoots arrows at adventurers or monsters,
which miss, and accumulate at the location of the
trap, they are of mixed composition: some may be
poisoned, some not, some may be blessed, or
uncursed, or cursed, some may be enchanted, some
not.

Yet, when the adventurer disarms the trap, all of
the remaining ammunition is of a single, stackable
type.

This defies common sense, that a trap should be
emitting multiple types of ammunition from a stock
which is all of one type. The uncharitable might
call it (horrors) a "bug".

YANI: remnant ammunition from a disarmed projectile
weapon (rock, dart, or arrow) trap should have the
same mix of diverse qualities as the projectiles the
trap emits, being dropped and given those qualities
by the game mechanics one by one when the trap is
disarmed, rather than all dropped in one homogeneous
stack.

